-- Backfill `wallet_dict.is_proxy` for every address already in the dictionary
-- that no keypair can sign for.
--
-- 0014 added the column and the live rule that keeps it current (a wallet
-- observed signing nothing on its own transaction is a proxy). That rule only
-- ever sees NEW trades. The rows already written — 462,483 of them — were
-- ingested without the signer test, so their proxies have to be identified from
-- the addresses themselves.
--
-- THE TEST. An Ed25519 public key is a point on the curve. A program-derived
-- address is chosen precisely because it is NOT, so that no private key exists
-- for it. Decompressing each of `wallet_dict`'s addresses and asking whether it
-- lands on the curve therefore partitions the dictionary into "could sign" and
-- "provably cannot", using nothing but the 32 bytes — no transaction, no log, no
-- retained payload. That is what makes it applicable to history the feed has
-- long since dropped.
--
-- THE RESULT, on the workstation dictionary at the time of writing: 930 of
-- 1,362,485 addresses are off-curve, 814 of them carry trades, and those 814
-- carry 462,483 rows. One address is 427,767 of that total —
-- `ARu4n5mFdZogZAravu7CcizaojWnS6oqka37gdLT5SZn`, a PDA of the OKX DEX Router,
-- and the single busiest entry in the whole table.
--
-- The list is spelled out rather than computed because Postgres has no Ed25519
-- point decompression, and a curve check in PL/pgSQL would be a second, drifting
-- implementation of a fact the ingest decoder already establishes exactly. It is
-- keyed by ADDRESS, not by `wallet_dict.id`, so it applies identically on every
-- database regardless of interning order; an address absent from a given
-- dictionary simply matches nothing.
--
-- NOT EVERY ENTRY IS A ROUTER PROXY. Some are protocol vaults or pool
-- authorities that genuinely move tokens on chain. None of them is a person, so
-- excluding all of them from wallet-level study is right either way.
--
-- This is a snapshot of a computed property, not a registry to maintain by hand.
-- Addresses interned after it are covered by the live `is_proxied` rule from
-- 0014; re-run the off-curve sweep only if that rule is ever bypassed.

